A||||5||Cooter||Engine replaced????||||1||
Z||000000||Cooter||04-30-2000||12:53 AM||||Today I began pulling all the bolt on stuff from my GT's 180,000 mile engine. After removing the valve covers, I saw the inside of the engine is cleaner than the 3.4 that is going back in. The hone marks are still very clear in the cylinders (as viewed from the bottom). How can I tell if this is the original engine or it has been replaced? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mshill||04-30-2000||01:10 AM||||I wouldn't be surprised.  My 86SE had 190K original miles on it (previous owner kept all receipts) and it also had the original hone crosshatch marks on all six cylinders and very clean.<P>Don't know how you can tell if you don't have records for it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||04-30-2000||02:54 AM||||Isn't there a number on the block that should match the build number in the car's VIN?||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||04-30-2000||09:05 AM||||I believe there is an single letter engine code within the VIN (somebody correct me if I'm wrong). For example "R", trouble is they may of used the "R" engine in several different GM models and years. If it happened that the code didn't match, then you'd know for sure it wasn't original. Cooter, maybe it was rebuilt? Does it have standard size pistons and bearings?<P>I justed checked, it's the 8th digit in the VIN that is the engine code, but I think there were only 2 or 3 different style 2.8 engines, so even if they put a different one in, it could very well be they put one in with the correct code<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 04-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdm1964||04-30-2000||10:30 AM||||The vin number of the car is stamped on the back side of the block near the starter. Just above the starter, on the flat spot towards the trans.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroshop||04-30-2000||11:08 AM||||I've seen several engines that were real clean when removed and I've seen engines that were full of crap. It all depends how the previous motor was taken care of and what kind of oil.||||reg||1
